    <string name="about_does_muxlume_include_channels">Does MUXLUME include channels?</string>
    <string name="about_no_muxlume_is_a_player">No. MUXLUME is a player. You add playlists or provider accounts you\'re authorized to use; nothing is bundled or sold.</string>
    <string name="about_a_channel_doesn_t_play">A channel doesn\'t play</string>
    <string name="about_open_the_player_s_info">Open the player\'s info panel (the sliders icon) to see the error. Common causes: the provider\'s connection limit is reached, the channel is offline, or the stream uses a codec this device can\'t decode. Refreshing the playlist fixes moved channels.</string>
    <string name="about_unencrypted_http_errors">\"Unencrypted HTTP\" errors</string>
    <string name="about_streams_over_http_are_blocked">Streams over http:// are blocked until you allow them. Edit the playlist in Library and tick \"allow unencrypted HTTP\". Prefer https:// if your provider offers it.</string>
    <string name="about_import_failed_or_is_slow">Import failed or is slow</string>
    <string name="about_very_large_playlists_take_a">Very large playlists take a while; the import can be cancelled and your previous list stays intact. If it fails, the reason is shown on the playlist\'s card in Library.</string>
    <string name="about_which_formats_work">Which formats work?</string>
    <string name="about_hls_m3u8_mpeg_dash_mpd">HLS (.m3u8), MPEG-DASH (.mpd), RTSP and progressive files such as MPEG-TS, MP4 and MKV, as far as this device\'s decoders support the codecs. DRM-protected streams and RTMP are not supported.</string>
    <string name="about_where_is_the_tv_guide">Where is the TV guide?</string>
    <string name="about_the_electronic_program_guide_xmltv">Open Live TV and tap the calendar icon. The guide is off until you turn it on for a playlist (when adding it, or in Settings → TV guide). It needs a guide link: yours, or the one your playlist announces. Xtream playlists use the provider\'s own guide. Reminders need notification permission.</string>
